  "body": "With its wide Gulf view, premium address, big swimming pool & plenty of possibilities - this substantial family home presents an exceptional opportunity to make it your own.\r\n\r\nFor 36 years, this impressive John D'Anvers-designed home has been the much-loved base for its current owners. Now it's time for a new family to take it into its next chapter.\r\n\r\nAnd what a location to do it from.\r\n\r\nSet in a highly sought-after coastal neighbourhood, you're close to two popular beaches, scenic coastal walkways, sought-after Rangitoto College school zone, and a host of everyday amenities, with transport options close at hand. It's the sort of location that makes life easy - whether it's a morning walk by the water, a swim at the beach, the school run or simply enjoying everything the area has to offer.\r\n\r\nBuilt in the 1980s and spread across three levels, the home offers the space and flexibility that growing families, extended families and buyers looking for something a little different will appreciate. Whether you're looking for a substantial family home, somewhere to accommodate different generations, a property with scope to add value, or simply a great lifestyle location with an enviable outlook, this one deserves a closer look.\r\n\r\nUpstairs is the private master retreat, with a generous bedroom, ensuite and adjoining office or nursery. The outlook is exceptional, with commanding views across the Gulf.\r\n\r\nThe spacious lounge and dining area opens to a deck, again with a sweeping outlook across the gulf, while on the opposite side another deck takes in the outlook over the large inground pool. The kitchen is conveniently positioned alongside additional, more casual, dining space, with a handy powder room completing this well-proportioned living and entertaining area.\r\n\r\nDownstairs is all about family living, with three bedrooms, a generous family room, bathroom and separate toilet. French doors open directly from this living zone to the pool area, creating an easy indoor-outdoor connection. The downstairs toilet also has direct access from the pool - perfect for those inevitable wet feet without having to traipse through the living areas.\r\n\r\nThe 981sqm (more or lesss) site is fully fenced at the rear, with plenty of space for children, pets, entertaining and poolside enjoyment. A separate double garage with automatic door adds practical storage and parking.\r\n\r\nFor its next owners, there is now an opportunity to refresh and personalise the interiors, bringing their own style and contemporary touches to a home that has been such an important part of one family's story for so long.\r\n\r\nThere may also be potential to subdivide, subject to Council approval and all necessary requirements - adding another dimension to the property's appeal.\r\n\r\nAfter 36 years, this much-loved home oozes potential and is ready for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nA sought-after coastal location. An exceptional outlook. Serious family space. And with plenty of opportunity to make it your own.\r\n\r\nDeadline sale date: 4pm Tuesday 8 December 2026 (unless sold prior)",
